{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0ef88ebf0d44464fb33be14314bcc850f864d5707c636241c40f4ef3f10a6116"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: managed home-directory files must be edited under dotfiles/ (mapped via hal_dotfiles.json), and skills/plugins edits only go live after publishing with a version bump since Claude Code loads them from the GitHub marketplace."},{"claim_ids":["clm_943e46197059f388004f40a59903f617d0d84710857ddb792e0a432ec093ec05"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors should use `make help` to find targets and prefer Makefile targets over running underlying tools directly; `make test` runs tests and `make hal-completion` regenerates zsh completion after editing bin/hal.py."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0ef88ebf0d44464fb33be14314bcc850f864d5707c636241c40f4ef3f10a6116","clm_943e46197059f388004f40a59903f617d0d84710857ddb792e0a432ec093ec05"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_04a9cd62a1c4424f83980bf52ad0b8f6","id":"pg_8cfbcdb2f86a541696c9956b3e4eee0b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/vinta-hal-9000-claude-md-0485a6495f80-956b3e4eee0b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_0baafc4bd7b25d7a99fd8922a4ba9907"],"title":"vinta/hal-9000/CLAUDE.md @ 0485a6495f80","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_04a9cd62a1c4424f83980bf52ad0b8f6"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_01aab0119d6b225e1aec9585665838c41ab5364e7ab9d40f11a48c89e73deabf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The `hal` CLI supports subcommands including update (with --tags), link/unlink, sync (--force), backup (--prune), restore, and open-the-pod-bay-doors."},{"claim_ids":["clm_16b1d164383d255a885856d9fbc751989fd220ecf423e4ef356c995269de243e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Claude Code plugins include hal-output-styles, hal-session-auto-rename (auto-renames sessions as conversations evolve), and hal-voice (plays HAL 9000 voice clips on hook events)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_53eadc8c74abc166fc6b3ee2668291610d4cec0140221004ae65973798993cad"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is named after the HAL 9000 computer from Arthur C. Clarke's 2001: A Space Odyssey."},{"claim_ids":["clm_813ff1b8d757e533f1bdae8e485c592f56a785e4d17727f108211e1d2edb9d85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Dotfiles include configs for Claude Code settings, Codex, Ghostty, uv, npm, and zsh, described as hardened against supply chain attacks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_86e2cdb644da97d4b7b129877b203468e34156029db68bbcd084e142db64c855"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A one-line bootstrap command pipes bin/open-the-pod-bay-doors.sh from GitHub into bash."},{"claim_ids":["clm_943e46197059f388004f40a59903f617d0d84710857ddb792e0a432ec093ec05"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors should use `make help` to find targets and prefer Makefile targets over running underlying tools directly; `make test` runs tests and `make hal-completion` regenerates zsh completion after editing bin/hal.py."},{"claim_ids":["clm_987e830cf38de163c0c36a51cb8a6484571b8011169a4ddf8b42a9199e243767"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project describes itself as an opinionated AI coding agent and dev environment automation tool for macOS."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c17f00a74a43c60cf6cebf827abbc7f347bbdcb35a3ddf0fad346dd2014e6943"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The hal-statusline plugin shows the current model, directory, git branch, and model usage, and adds a grammar check on typed prompts with Traditional Chinese explanations."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e8e7517c3903cc6744877ddbe3af3598706c1b43508b25c486c2b9e87b1f85d3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The bootstrap step installs agent skills, Claude Code configs/plugins/rules/statusline, Codex configs, and Ansible roles for Python, Node.js, Bun, Solidity, Docker, Kubernetes, AWS, and Google Cloud."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ee27e9d1c34e1f309b532158d80f654b2fb01986361d9dd8a49cc138fc364abf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repo ships agentic skills such as commit (atomic conventional commits), pr, best-practices, blindspot, simple-english, write-like-me, and several refactor/audit skills."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f781f64ef851ae204fcb28fe4b50825e1b31b02ca364b804070a8192134a6c09"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills can be installed into Claude Code via a plugin marketplace command, or into Codex and other agents via `npx skills add vinta/hal-9000`."}],"claim_ids":["clm_01aab0119d6b225e1aec9585665838c41ab5364e7ab9d40f11a48c89e73deabf","clm_16b1d164383d255a885856d9fbc751989fd220ecf423e4ef356c995269de243e","clm_53eadc8c74abc166fc6b3ee2668291610d4cec0140221004ae65973798993cad","clm_813ff1b8d757e533f1bdae8e485c592f56a785e4d17727f108211e1d2edb9d85","clm_86e2cdb644da97d4b7b129877b203468e34156029db68bbcd084e142db64c855","clm_943e46197059f388004f40a59903f617d0d84710857ddb792e0a432ec093ec05","clm_987e830cf38de163c0c36a51cb8a6484571b8011169a4ddf8b42a9199e243767","clm_c17f00a74a43c60cf6cebf827abbc7f347bbdcb35a3ddf0fad346dd2014e6943","clm_e8e7517c3903cc6744877ddbe3af3598706c1b43508b25c486c2b9e87b1f85d3","clm_ee27e9d1c34e1f309b532158d80f654b2fb01986361d9dd8a49cc138fc364abf","clm_f781f64ef851ae204fcb28fe4b50825e1b31b02ca364b804070a8192134a6c09"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:30:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_04a9cd62a1c4424f83980bf52ad0b8f6","id":"pg_b71dfa22e7cf50e2b1cccdcb28e1